<title>ITALY: Italy's Stet must pay state 120 bln lire.</title>
<headline>Italy's Stet must pay state 120 bln lire.</headline>
<dateline>ROME 1997-01-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Italian telecommunications holding Stet must pay the state 120 billion lire ($74.9 million) as part of a complex balancing act involving Italy's two mobile phone operators, Post and Telecommunications Minister Antonio Maccanico said.</p>
<p>As a result of this payment, Italy's second mobile phone company, Omnitel, will not now receive 60 billion lire in reimbursements from Stet's operating units, Maccanico told a parliamentary commission. ($ = 1602 Italian Lire)</p>
</text>
